ined on billions of in vivo non-human primate (NHP) measurements, Dyno's platform engineers AAV capsids optimized for selective delivery, liver detargeting, cross-species translatability and manufacturability.\" SUPPORTED.\n\n9. p2:c3 — quote found verbatim. SUPPORTED.\n\n10. p2:c4 — quote found verbatim: \"Phi now enables therapeutic developers to run frontier open-weight protein structure models, applying filters and experimentally calibrated reasoning to support genetic medicine development\". SUPPORTED.\n\n11. p2:done — quote found verbatim in yp2 page. SUPPORTED.\n\n12. p3:step — Nature page: \"Here, we adapt an unbiased human cell microarray platform to determine the extracellular and cell surface interactomes of natural and engineered AAVs.\" — found in abstract. Item also mentions capsid–receptor interactome on brain endothelium-relevant receptors such as LRP6 — yes LRP6 BBB transcytosis. SUPPORTED.\n\n13. p3:activity — DOI resolved to a citation listing: \"Brittain, T. J., ... (2026). Structural basis of liver de-targeting and neuronal tropism of CNS-targeted AAV capsids. Molecular Therapy, 34(7), 3820–3837.\" The recorded quote \"Overall, we provide a framework for using structural information to guide rational engineering...\" is not on this page — it's just a bibliography entry. The fetch only returned a citation. Hmm, that page seems to be some index page. The item claims publication 28 March 2026 and quote. The DOI page fetched confirms article exists with that title (supporting activity's core claim but not the quote). Lin et al. Cell Reports 31 Oct 2025 not verified (Sci Adv 2023 paper is my earlier knowledge; the CA-IV paper was Sci Adv eadg6618 in 2023, not Cell Reports Oct 2025 — actually Shay et al 2023 Sci Adv was CA-IV. The item says \"Lin et al. in Cell Reports (31 October 2025) on human CA-IV-targeted AAVs\" — unverified). I'd mark PARTIAL: DOI page confirms the Brittain 2026 Molecular Therapy paper exists with matching title; the recorded quote is not on the page, and the Lin et al. claim unverified. Actually the fetch returned literally only a citation; date 28 March 2026 not shown. PARTIAL seems right.\n\n14. p3:c1 — quote verbatim: \"After these controls, we then tested the six-capsid pool in a full screen of over 6400 proteins, including 6019 human plasma membrane proteins and secreted and cell surface-tethered proteins, as well as 397 heterodimers.\" Matching \"over 90% membrane proteome\" also in text (\"This unbiased screen includes more than 90% of the human membrane proteome and secretome\"). OUTPUT however said \">84%\". SUPPORTED.\n\n15. p3:c2 — quote verbatim: \"We applied AlphaFold-Multimer to build models of LRP6-AAV interaction complexes, which predicted that the X1 and CAP-Mac VR-VIII peptides bind LRP6 YWTD domain 1 (Fig. 4c).\" The item says \"5 structural models per peptide\" — Fig 4 caption: \"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles\". SUPPORTED.\n\n16. p3:c3 — quote verbatim: \"While the cooperative folding of E1 and E2 complicates testing of individual domains, SPR of mouse LRP6 extracellular domain fragments was consistent with the model predictions, with interaction observed for LRP6-E1E2 but not LRP6-E3E4 (Fig. 4d).\" SUPPORTED.\n\n17. p3:c4 — sourced to ymthe.2026.03.030 — page only gave citation, not the cryo-EM 2.22/2.20 Å quote. UNREACHABLE for the quote. Hmm, fetch returned only a bibliographic listing. Try fetching the ScienceDirect page? The doi redirected to something producing just a citation line. Maybe try again with the sciencedirect URL or search. Let me attempt a search for the Brittain paper cryo-EM 2.22 Å.\n\n18. p3:c5 — quote verbatim: \"Finally, we functionally validate LRP6 capsid interactions in vivo in mice, in the human BBB via primary cell culture, and beyond the BBB using human pluripotent stem cell (hPSC)-derived neurons.\" Item mentions Lrp6 conditional knockout mice, human and ma